    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0584" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/17760</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Representative Rodgers to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Querétaro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-05T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1916, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. In relation to Northwestern Railway. Although, after long conference early
                    this morning, promised reply to-day, none has been forthcoming. Appears
                    deliberate evasion. Think instructions as requested and promised will issue
                    finally, but present attitude very unsatisfactory. This morning was asked for
                    names of consignees supplies. This evidently for purpose of delay. Informed them
                    would not ask for names, our agreement being observed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rodgers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
